# Contributing

Thanks for helping with {{PROJECT_NAME}}.

## Issues

Open an issue with one of the forms: a bug report, an improvement, a feature request or a
documentation problem. For a larger change, open an issue first, so we can agree on the
approach. Report security vulnerabilities privately, as the
[security policy](https://github.com/{{REPOSITORY}}/security/policy) describes.

## Development

`AGENTS.md` describes how the project is built and tested. Before you send a pull request,
make sure this passes:

    scripts/check.sh

## Commits and pull requests

Commit messages follow Conventional Commits
(https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/). Keep a pull request to one change, with
tests for the new behavior, and fill in the pull request template.

